---
description: Public repo — never commit paper-specific or review-specific content
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository is public. Commit pipeline code, generic docs, and synthetic fixtures only.

Never commit content tied to a real paper or an under-review submission: PDFs, extracted text, quoted or paraphrased sentences, titles, figure or page images, table numbers, reviews, ratings, submission or forum ids, venue assignment, or reviewer identity.

Keep review inputs and outputs outside the repo in a gitignored directory (`workdir/`, `reviews/`, `papers/`, or `uploads/`).

Do not copy a manuscript into tests. Write a new synthetic fixture.

Do not put a leaked sentence into the denylist, commit message, or docs. Block exact strings only as SHA-256 digests in `scripts/confidentiality_hashes.txt`.

Run `python3 scripts/check_confidentiality.py` on tracked files. Do not force-push `main` to erase history; report the commit SHAs to the owner.
